The typosquat detection in `typosquat.py` is a port of RAPTOR's
`packages/sca/supply_chain/typosquat.py` — the algorithm (Damerau-Levenshtein with
a distance cap, the character-set prefilter and the length bucketing), the
severity thresholds and the bundled data under `data/` (popularity feeds per
ecosystem, the confusable denylist and the reviewed-legitimate allowlist) are
RAPTOR's work, redistributed under the MIT License. The data is trimmed to the
PyPI and npm ecosystems, which are the ones raptor-win parses.

